@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    Layout = "_PublicLayout";
}

<div class="policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Amateur Radio License Exam Session Management</p>

    <p class="policy-note">
        This page describes what personal information we collect when you register for an amateur
        radio license exam session, why we collect it, and how long we keep it. If you have questions
        about your information, contact the Volunteer Examiner team running your session.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you register for an exam session, we collect and store:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Name</strong> — to identify you at the session and on your exam paperwork</li>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> — to send session details, payment links, and result notifications</li>
        <li><strong>FCC Registration Number (FRN)</strong> — required to submit your exam results to the FCC</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Session administration</strong> — confirming your registration, sending Zoom/meeting details, and tracking attendance</li>
        <li><strong>FCC application tracking</strong> — matching your exam results to your FCC application and license grant</li>
        <li><strong>Payment processing</strong> — generating and tracking payment for exam fees</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    @if (Model.PiiRetentionWindowDays is int days)
    {
        <p>
            We retain your personal information for <strong>@days days</strong> after the relevant
            outcome of your exam: for candidates who pass, @days days after your license is granted
            by the FCC; for candidates who do not pass, @days days after your exam date. After that
            window, your name, email, and felony-disclosure answer are permanently removed from our
            records. If you do not test (e.g. a no-show or withdrawal), this information is removed
            immediately.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p>
            Our data retention window is currently being finalized. Personal information is retained
            only as long as needed to complete session administration, FCC application tracking, and
            payment processing described above, and is removed once no longer needed for those
            purposes.
        </p>
    }
    <p>
        Identifiers that are already part of the FCC's public record — your FCC Registration Number
        (FRN), call sign, and FCC license/application reference numbers — along with non-personal
        exam statistics (such as license grant date and pass/fail outcome) may be retained longer,
        for historical reporting and so your exam record stays traceable if a question about your
        application ever comes up.
    </p>

    @* The page promised candidates a retention window while saying nothing at all about VEs, whose
       home addresses it also holds (#313 / L-07). Both states are stated explicitly now, including
       the "kept indefinitely" one — an unstated indefinite hold is the thing worth avoiding. *@
    <h2>If you volunteer as an examiner</h2>
    <p>
        Volunteer Examiners give their team contact details — including a home address — so that
        sessions can be organized. This is separate from the address on your public FCC record, and
        we treat it that way: it is visible only to your team's administrators and to you, and it is
        never included in the public record we read back from the FCC.
    </p>
    @if (Model.VeContactRetentionYears is int veYears)
    {
        <p>
            If you stop volunteering — no active team roster membership, and no session worked for
            <strong>@veYears years</strong> — we clear your email address, phone number, home
            address, Discord username and any notes about you. Your name, call sign, FRN,
            accreditations and the record of sessions you worked are kept, because together they are
            the record that you were qualified to administer those exams.
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p>
            We currently keep Volunteer Examiner contact details for as long as the record exists.
            Ask your team's administrators if you would like yours removed.
        </p>
    }
</div>
